    "finalAnswer": "I fixed the bug in `truncate` in `src/lib/strings.js`, and all 13 tests now pass.\n\n**The bug:** `truncate` kept the first `max` characters and then added the ellipsis, so the result came out longer than `max`. For example, `truncate('abcdefghij', 5)` returned `'abcde…'`, which is 6 characters.\n\n**The fix:** one line now leaves room for the ellipsis:\n\n```js\nreturn text.slice(0, max - ellipsis.length) + ellipsis;\n```\n\nThe same call now returns `'abcd…'`, which is what the test expects. I didn't touch the tests.",
